
📊 Week 8: Final Integration, Documentation & Project Deployment

In Week 8, the project was completed by focusing on final integration, documentation, and portfolio preparation. This phase ensured that all analysis, dashboards, and insights developed in previous weeks were properly organized and presented in a professional manner.

All components of the project—including data cleaning, exploratory analysis, KPI development, data modeling, and visualization—were integrated into a complete end-to-end solution. The final dashboard and insights were reviewed to ensure accuracy, consistency, and business relevance.

A major focus of this week was on project documentation using GitHub. The repository was structured systematically with separate folders for:

Dataset and processed data
Scripts and analysis files
Dashboard files (Power BI)
Documentation and reports

A well-documented README file was created, which plays a critical role in explaining the project. It includes sections such as project overview, KPIs, dashboard details, key insights, recommendations, and tools used. This helps make the project easy to understand for recruiters and collaborators.

Additionally, the project was prepared as a professional portfolio, demonstrating skills in data cleaning, EDA, data modeling, visualization, and business analysis. Proper version control and organization ensure scalability and easy maintenance.

The final outcome of this week is a complete, structured, and portfolio-ready data analytics project that showcases end-to-end capabilities—from raw data to actionable business insights—making it highly valuable for real-world applications and career opportunities.
